@startuml EnterpriseMLPlatformTrainingRegistrySequence

title Enterprise ML Platform - Training, Registration, Promotion and Rollback
autonumber

actor "ML engineer / pipeline" as User
participant "ModelTrainingService" as Training
participant "HyperparameterOptimizer" as Optimizer
participant "Trainer\n(XGBoost / LightGBM / Ensemble)" as Trainer
participant "ModelExplainer" as Explainer
participant "MLflow tracking" as Tracking
participant "MLflow artifact store" as Artifacts
participant "MLflowModelRegistry" as Registry
participant "MLflow Model Registry" as MLflowRegistry
participant "Serving model loader" as Serving

== Train and evaluate ==

User -> Training: train(X, y, config, X_val, y_val)

opt hyperparameter optimization configured
    Training -> Optimizer: optimize(trainer factory, X, y, search config)
    Optimizer --> Training: best parameters
end

Training -> Trainer: train(...)
Trainer --> Training: trained model
Training -> Trainer: evaluate(model, validation data)
Trainer --> Training: metrics

opt explainability configured
    Training -> Explainer: explain(model, X, explainability config)
    Explainer --> Training: explanation outputs
end

== Track immutable training evidence ==

alt MLflow tracking enabled
    Training -> Tracking: start explicit experiment run
    Training -> Tracking: log parameters + metrics
    Training -> Tracking: log drift-reference metadata
    Training -> Artifacts: log serialized model artifact
    Artifacts --> Training: model URI
    Tracking --> Training: run ID
else tracking disabled
    Training -> Training: return model + metrics only
end

Training --> User: model + metrics

== Register an immutable model version ==

User -> Registry: register(name, model URI, tags, description)
Registry -> MLflowRegistry: register model artifact
MLflowRegistry --> Registry: immutable version N
Registry --> User: ModelVersionInfo(name, N, run_id, source)

== Promote deployment intent ==

User -> Registry: promote(name, N, alias="champion")
Registry -> MLflowRegistry: move champion alias -> version N
MLflowRegistry --> Registry: alias updated
Registry --> User: promoted version metadata

note over Registry,MLflowRegistry
Promotion changes registry metadata only.
The immutable model artifact and version N do not change.
end note

== Load for serving ==

Serving -> Registry: resolve champion alias
Registry -> MLflowRegistry: get version by alias
MLflowRegistry --> Registry: exact immutable version N
Registry --> Serving: models:/name/N + drift reference

note over Serving
Serving resolves the alias during model load.
Prediction requests then use the cached immutable
version until another load occurs.
end note

== Roll back ==

User -> Registry: rollback(name, alias="champion")
Registry -> MLflowRegistry: read current champion version N
Registry -> MLflowRegistry: list older immutable versions
MLflowRegistry --> Registry: versions N-1, N-2, ...
Registry -> MLflowRegistry: move champion alias -> newest older version
MLflowRegistry --> Registry: alias updated
Registry --> User: rollback target metadata

note over Registry,MLflowRegistry
Rollback also moves only the alias.
No historical artifact is mutated or retrained.
end note

@enduml
